<title>MEXICO: Mexico businessman Crescencio Ballesteros dies.</title>
<headline>Mexico businessman Crescencio Ballesteros dies.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-07-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The honorary chairman of Mexican construction company Grupo Mexicano de Desarrollo SA (GMD) died at 83 late Friday of heart failure, his publicist said in a statement.</p>
<p>Crescencio Ballesteros Ibarra founded GMD in 1975, and his son Jose Luis is current president of the company. Ballesteros also once owned Mexicana de Aviacion SA, now part of holding company Cintra SA, and owned a controlling share of holding company Synkro SA.</p>
<p>Ballesteros served on the board of directors of more than 20 Mexican firms, among them Kimberly-Clark de Mexico SA and Desc SA, the statement said.</p>
<p>He was buried on Saturday in Mexico City.</p>
<p>((-- Timna Tanners, Mexico City newsroom +525 728-7903))</p>
